Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.50,0:00:04.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}I'm [Name];\NI led data quality and preparation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.90,0:00:06.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}I profiled before cleaning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.74,0:00:13.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}NHANES stores 'refused' and 'don't know'\Nas numeric codes such as 7, 9, 77 and 99.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.01,0:00:16.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The common shortcut sets those values\Nto missing in every column.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.65,0:00:22.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}That catches 57 genuine codes,\Nand destroys 1,496 valid measurements,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.52,0:00:26.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}including HbA1c\Nvalues of exactly 7.0 percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.30,0:00:32.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Each 7.0 is above the 6.5 threshold:\Na diabetes case.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.48,0:00:37.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The shortcut erased 29 of 721\NHbA1c-based positives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.69,0:00:40.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Only six changed label;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.15,0:00:44.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}the rest had also self-reported,\Nso the either-or label hid the damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.01,0:00:45.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}No summary statistic shows this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.30,0:00:47.53,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Second, outliers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.53,0:00:52.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The 1.5 times IQR rule\Nflags 542 HbA1c values.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.33,0:00:55.69,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Its upper fence lies above\Nthe diagnostic threshold,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.69,0:01:01.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}so the 519 high values are diabetes\Nby definition: the disease, not errors.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.14,0:01:02.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}We reviewed and kept them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.50,0:01:07.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}[Name]'s exploration\Nfound redundancy and skew.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.20,0:01:10.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Weight and BMI show\Nsevere multicollinearity:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.16,0:01:14.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}variance inflation factors\Nof 95.7 and 97.6.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.25,0:01:19.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Fasting triglycerides are strongly\Nright-skewed: skewness 6.62.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.29,0:01:22.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Both matter for a linear model,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.04,0:01:25.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}so the systematic preparation drops weight\Nand applies a Yeo-Johnson transform,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.91,0:01:27.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}which brings the skewness close to zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.30,0:01:31.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Each finding became a switchable step,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.10,0:01:36.05,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}fourteen in all, each tied\Nto its evidence, and none reads the label.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.10,0:01:40.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}From them we built three\Nversions of the data.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.42,0:01:42.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Naive keeps every column.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.67,0:01:48.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Minimal adds one rule: drop items\Nthat exist only after a diagnosis,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.68,0:01:50.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}such as treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.14,0:01:52.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Systematic adds my other steps,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.68,0:01:56.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}from per-variable recoding\Nto transforms and class weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.79,0:02:00.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}All three feed the same model\Non the same folds.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.30,0:02:02.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Most unexpected for me:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.97,0:02:07.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}one routine cleaning line erased\N29 diabetic HbA1c results,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.60,0:02:08.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}and the label hid it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.17,0:02:12.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}But cleaning cannot fix the label itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.72,0:02:13.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}[Name] shows why.
